{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the two lotteries. To compute this, we compare each outcome in Lottery A with each outcome in Lottery B. The outcomes are: A1 = -6000 (0.1%), A2 = 0 (99.9%); B1 = -3000 (0.2%), B2 = 0 (99.8%). The pairwise outcome differences are: (-6000) - (-3000) = -3000; (-6000) - 0 = -6000; 0 - (-3000) = +3000; 0 - 0 = 0. The sum of these differences is -3000 + (-6000) + 3000 + 0 = -6000. Since the sum is negative, the reason would favor Lottery B, as it has the more favorable (less negative) sum of pairwise outcome differences. Thus, the decision reason is applicable to the decision problem, and it would prefer Lottery B.",
